# Line endings are normalized to LF in the working tree on every platform, not
# just in the repository.
#
# Without this, `npm run db:schema:check` fails on any Windows clone. Git's
# core.autocrlf=true — the default from Git for Windows and on GitHub's Windows
# runners — rewrites the checked-out schema to CRLF, while the header that
# scripts/build-schema.js compares it against is built from "\n" literals in
# JavaScript. The comparison is byte-for-byte, so it reports every schema as out
# of date on a tree nobody touched.
#
# The same applies to the shell in .github/workflows and to scripts run with
# bash: a CRLF line ending becomes part of the command, and the error that
# produces names a file that looks correct in an editor.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so no end-of-line conversion and no attempt to diff as text. These are
# gitignored, but a stray commit of one should not be silently corrupted by
# newline translation.
*.db binary
*.db-journal binary
*.sqlite binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
